{"items":[
{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"Illumina's own end-of-life policy bars service contracts on resold end-of-sale or end-of-life instruments. A third-party aftermarket cannot prop up a retired 6000 tail.","detail":"Policy CN 1107421 (effective 18 Jul 2024) says pre-owned End-of-Sale/End-of-Life instruments 'are not eligible for service contracts' except for a title transfer without relocation, or an M&A transfer. Approval for service on resold units needs the Regional GM and is granted 'only in extraordinary circumstances'. This fits the search finding of no independent service vendor for the 6000. It means that once a 6000 end-of-sale notice is issued, the clock on the tail becomes hard.","url":"https://emea.illumina.com/content/dam/illumina-marketing/documents/terms-conditions/1000000117071_01_Product_End_of_Sale_End_of_Life_Policy.pdf","date":"2024-07-18","source_name":"Illumina Product End-of-Life Policy 1000000117071 v01","source_type":"filing","quote":"not eligible for service contracts","strength":"medium","why_new":"Known list covers the retirement page and MiSeq dates, not the policy's resale-service bar or the pricing mechanics."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"Illumina's end-of-life policy mechanics give a firm timetable once a 6000 notice is issued: 5 years of service after the notice, with service prices rising from the notice date.","detail":"The policy says the End-of-Service-Life date 'typically will be five (5) years after the End-of-Life notice date' for RUO and Dx instruments, and it can be shorter. The Last Ship date comes 2–6 months after the end-of-sale notice for RUO instruments and at least 6 months for Dx. Service contract offers 'are subject to price increases from the End-of-Life notice date'. Contracts are renewable only up to 12 months before EOSL, and Illumina may discontinue individual consumable kits earlier if demand is low. A mid-2027 notice would imply EOSL around mid-2032. This is a more formal basis than the earlier extrapolation of service to ~2031–32, and it adds the consumable-kit discontinuation risk.","url":"https://emea.illumina.com/content/dam/illumina-marketing/documents/terms-conditions/1000000117071_01_Product_End_of_Sale_End_of_Life_Policy.pdf","date":"2024-07-18","source_name":"Illumina Product End-of-Life Policy","source_type":"filing","quote":"five (5) years after the End-of-Life notice date","strength":"medium","why_new":"The earlier 2031–32 date was labeled our extrapolation. This is the policy text behind it, plus the kit-discontinuation and service-price-increase terms."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"The used 6000 market is distressed: a retired, working US university-surplus unit is on sale at $30,000, half of its $60,000 regular price.","detail":"The MSU Surplus Store page shows an Illumina NovaSeq 6000 'used and in good physical condition', retired from a working lab, with the computer wiped, two APCs, an as-is sale and local pickup only. It shows a $60,000 regular price and a $30,000 sale price (−50%), against a ~$985K list. The probe saw $60K, so the markdown is new. Product image timestamps suggest about Aug 2025, so the unit has been unsold for about a year. That means a roughly 97% discount to list and no apparent buyer demand for 6000s outside Illumina-serviced fleets.","url":"https://msusurplusstore.com/products/illumina-novaseq-sequencing-system","date":"2026 (listing undated; images ~Aug 2025)","source_name":"MSU Surplus Store, SKU 150822","source_type":"price_list","quote":"Item is used and in good physical condition","strength":"medium","why_new":"Known list has $30K–$99K used units generally. This is the specific 50% markdown on a named unit plus its age on the market."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"A 2018-built 6000 is listed in the UK at £8,000 for spares or repair, with the control software failing at 94% initialisation.","detail":"UniGreenScheme (Universal Resource Trading) lists the unit at £8,000 ex-VAT (£9,600 inc.). It powers on, is cosmetically good, and has a PAT test dated 24 Nov 2025. A second listing at £7,950 was seen in search results only. At £8K the unit is about 1% of the $985K launch price. Software faults on an 8-year-old unit that no third party services point to Illumina-only repair, which supports the view that the 6000 base shrinks through scrapping.","url":"https://shop.unigreenscheme.co.uk/biotechnology/genomics/sequencing/dna-sequencers/illumina-novaseq-6000-dna-sequencer","date":"2025-11 (PAT test date)","source_name":"UniGreenScheme listing","source_type":"price_list","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"Adds a dated, named, fault-described unit to the generic used-price range already known."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"Government buyers explicitly justify Illumina-only 6000 service by saying third-party providers do not exist or are too slow, so there is no independent aftermarket.","detail":"The CDC sole-source notice (posted 10 Oct 2024, covering 7 Dec 2024–6 Dec 2025, est. $144,910.12 for NovaSeq 6000 plus MiSeq) calls third-party service insufficient because of 'longer timelines and procedural delays'. The Navy NMRC notice (22 Dec 2025) cites market research 'confirming the absence of alternative service providers'. Per a search snippet, it prices the Silver plan at $141,313. The NCI notice (14 Aug 2026) is sole-source under FAR 6.302-1. Illumina keeps 100% of 6000 service revenue at these accounts, at roughly $140–145K per box per year.","url":"https://console.sweetspotgov.com/federal-contracts/3fe396bd-4010-5305-b055-174a2bb9bf3b","date":"2024-10-10","source_name":"SweetspotGov / SAM notice (CDC); GovContractFinder (Navy, NCI)","source_type":"procurement","quote":"third-party services insufficient","strength":"medium","why_new":"Known list has the Navy, NCI and NIEHS notices. The CDC dollar estimate, the third-party wording and the NMRC $141K figure are new."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"against","claim":"The 6000 service stream is still renewed at roughly $140–145K per box per year, and in 2025 a CDC bundle (NovaSeq 6000 plus MiSeq) cost $144.9K, so no federal buyer is retiring the 6000 early.","detail":"Per-box 6000 service of about $141K (Navy, 2025/26 snippet) and about $144.9K for the CDC bundle (Dec 2024–Dec 2025) is steady with prior-year NMRC awards of $141–146K already known. Agencies are paying for another full year of service rather than letting contracts lapse or dropping to Bronze. The NCI notice in Aug 2026 covers preventive maintenance only. This weakly cuts against the thesis that the 6000 tail is being wound down fast.","url":"https://govcontractfinder.com/contracts/comprehensive-full-service-maintenance-repair-plan-for-illum-N3239826Q4072","date":"2025-12-22","source_name":"GovContractFinder (Navy NMRC N3239826Q4072)","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"Adds the CDC dollar amount and a 2024–26 series. The known list has only the NMRC $141–146K."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"A federal 6000 service solicitation (NIA, Mar 2025) was posted as full and open, but it still required certified Illumina technicians, so the market is effectively sole-source.","detail":"Solicitation 75N95025Q00163 (posted 5 Mar 2025, closed 19 Mar, performance 13 Apr–12 Oct 2025, a six-month term) requires 'certified Illumina technicians', parts, labor, travel, a 4-hour remote response and a 3-day on-site target. The six-month period is unusual against the annual cycles elsewhere. It suggests a bridge contract, possibly for a 6000 on its way out at the NIA, though that is an inference.","url":"https://console.sweetspotgov.com/federal-contracts/1c92e665-2c5c-5408-9c47-2cfafa04c0b5","date":"2025-03-05","source_name":"SweetspotGov / SAM (NIH, NIA Baltimore)","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"Not in the known list. It is an NIA six-month 6000 service contract in 2025."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"NCI Frederick runs a mixed fleet and is renewing 6000 service alongside X Plus, suggesting parallel running at a federal lab.","detail":"Solicitation M26-159 (period 21 Jan 2026–20 Jan 2027, proposals due 1 Dec 2025) covers 8 line items: a NovaSeq 6000 (A01063) on a Gold plan, a MiSeq, a NextSeq X Plus (LH00236), a NovaSeq X Plus (LH00551), and two DRAGEN servers with level-2 licences. The mix is 1 six-thousand-series unit against 2 X-series units among 4 sequencers. This is a legacy 6000 kept under the top-tier plan next to new X systems.","url":"https://frederick.cancer.gov/work-us/vendors-subcontractors/business-opportunities/service-maintenance-agreement-illumina-lab-equipment","date":"2025-12-01","source_name":"NCI Frederick business opportunities","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"The known list has the Gold plan. The full fleet makeup (NovaSeq X Plus LH00551 and NextSeq X Plus) and the dates are new detail."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"supports","claim":"Illumina's end-of-life policy says it may discontinue individual consumable kits on a retiring instrument when demand is low, a lever that could force 6000 users to the X.","detail":"The policy says that during the EOL period Illumina should continue to supply consumables, but 'if demand is low and/or availability of materials is limited, Illumina may discontinue any individual Instrument Consumable kit(s) at any time'. It also says Illumina may 'allocate at its discretion' in cases of limited supply. This gives Illumina a lever to pull the 6000 tail onto X, but it may also trigger rivals' pitches (Novogene already ended 6000 support on 1 Jun 2025).","url":"https://emea.illumina.com/content/dam/illumina-marketing/documents/terms-conditions/1000000117071_01_Product_End_of_Sale_End_of_Life_Policy.pdf","date":"2024-07-18","source_name":"Illumina Product End-of-Life Policy","source_type":"filing","quote":"may discontinue any individual Instrument Consumable kit(s)","strength":"weak","why_new":"The policy text on kit discontinuation is not in the known list."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"Third-party resale does not produce a serviced 6000 secondary market, because Illumina reserves service priority and may refuse to restore operability on pre-owned boxes.","detail":"The policy lets Illumina weigh buyer purchase volume, existing install base and the business need for the instrument when deciding whether to serve a pre-owned instrument. It says it 'does not guarantee that a pre-owned … instrument can be restored to operability'. Combined with $8K–$60K asking prices and no ISO found, a buyer of a used 6000 relies on Illumina's goodwill for service and kits, which Illumina can deny. Illumina therefore controls whether the used-6000 market becomes a source of new low-volume consumables demand.","url":"https://emea.illumina.com/content/dam/illumina-marketing/documents/terms-conditions/1000000117071_01_Product_End_of_Sale_End_of_Life_Policy.pdf","date":"2024-07-18","source_name":"Illumina Product End-of-Life Policy","source_type":"filing","quote":"does not guarantee that a pre-owned","strength":"weak","why_new":"Not in the known list. It addresses whether the used market can extend the tail."}
